  "solution": "**BODMAS Rule:**\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/2042326d26ec7b593e52bbbdd22d890b59b1e59f92be81a7235509e9af1c4625.png] \n\nIf the numbers ‘18’ and ‘30’ are interchanged,\n\nLet check all options one by one.\n\nOption 1) 12 – 30 × 18 ÷ 3 + 16 = 174\n\nAfter interchanging the digit we get:\n\n⇒ 12 – 18 × __**30 ÷ 3**__ + 16 = 174\n\n⇒ 12 - __**18 × 10**__ + 16 = 174\n\n⇒ __**12**__ - 180 __**+ 16**__ = 174\n\n⇒ __**28 - 180**__ = 174\n\n⇒ - 152 ≠ 174\n\n⇒ **LHS ≠ RHS**\n\nOption 2) 14 × 5 – 18 ÷ 6 + 30 = 73\n\nAfter interchanging the digit we get:\n\n⇒ 14 × 5 – __**30 ÷ 6 **__+ 18 = 73\n\n⇒ __**14 × 5**__ - 5 + 18 = 73\n\n⇒ __**70**__ - 5 __**+ 18 **__= 73\n\n⇒ __**88 - 5**__ = 73\n\n⇒ 83 ≠ 73\n\n⇒ **LHS ≠ RHS**\n\nOption 3) 35 ÷ 5 × 5 + 30 – 18 = 23\n\nAfter interchanging the digit we get:\n\n⇒ __**35 ÷ 5**__ × 5 + 18 – 30 = 23\n\n⇒ __**7 × 5**__ + 18 - 30 = 23\n\n⇒ __**35 + 18**__ - 30 = 23\n\n⇒ __**53 - 30**__ = 23\n\n⇒ 23 = 23\n\n⇒ **LHS = RHS**\n\nOption 4) 64 + 18 × 5 ÷ 3 – 30 = 98\n\nAfter interchanging the digit we get:\n\n⇒ 64 + 30 × __**5 ÷ 3 **__– 18 = 98\n\n⇒ 64 + __**30 × 1.666**__ - 18 = 98\n\n⇒ __**64 + 49.98**__ - 18 = 98\n\n⇒ 113.98 - 18 = 98\n\n⇒ 95.98 ≠ 98\n\n⇒ **LHS ≠ RHS**\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"35 ÷ 5 × 5 + 30 – 18 = 23\".**",
